/Title (CityRouteFinderdemonstrates how graph data structures and shortest-path algorithms can solve a practical route-planning problem. The road network is stored as an adjacency list, with cities represented as vertices and roads represented as weighted, two-way edges.)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 369 0 R
/Next 827 0 R
>>
endobj
563 0 obj
<<
/Title (The sample test cases demonstrate normal route calculation, the same-city boundary case, invalid city handling and an alternate route after blocking a road. The project provides a foundation for future extensions such as dynamic road data, graphical maps and live traffic information.)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 369 0 R
/Prev 827 0 R
>>
